---
title: Ras el Hanout Slow-Roasted Mushrooms with Halloumi
source: Roasting Tin
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 1 hour 20 minutes
---

Preheat your oven to 130°C fan. Place @butter{70%g}(melted), @ras el hanout{4%tsp}, @lemon{1}(zest), and @garlic{4%clove}(crushed) in a #roasting tin{}. Transfer to the oven for ~{5%minutes} to melt the butter and allow the spices to toast a little.

Meanwhile, trim @mushrooms{600%g} and peel and halve @shallots{300%g}. After ~{5%minutes}, pop them into the tin with the melted spice butter, season well with @sea salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{}, and mix everything together really well with your hands. Cover in tinfoil, then place in the oven to cook for ~{60%minutes}.

After ~{60%minutes}, increase the heat to 150°C fan/170°C/gas 3 and remove the tinfoil. Squeeze over @lemon{1}(juice), add @halloumi{250%g}(cut into 1cm cubes), and mix well before scattering with @pine nuts{30%g}. Return to the oven to cook uncovered for a further ~{15%minutes}.

Taste and adjust the level of @sea salt{} as required, and scatter with @parsley{}(roughly chopped) and @pink peppercorns{2%tsp} just before serving.
